{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/841708-pitch-your-campaign","id":841708,"title":"Pitch your campaign!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-03T21:38:14-08:00","id":841708,"title":"Pitch your campaign!","content":"This isn't a recruitment thread, unless something really picks up interest. It's more for rapid fire throwing-out of all your ChroD campaign ideas, all the games you've wanted to run or play in. &quot;Pitches&quot; can be as long or as short as you want. <br /> <br /> Example: <br /> <br /> - In a fairly nice, quiet town called Princeton, you attended a fairly nice, quiet private high school called the Nadir Peak School of Princeton. You had a pretty average life- some hobbies, some friends, and so on. Sure, there were parts that didn't always make sense. Like when you realized your house didn't have an address. Or when you an A on your report card, but it didn't list any classes or anything else and the whole report card was just a blank sheet of paper with a large &quot;A&quot; written on it in marker. Or how your parents are physically identical and neither of them blink. But none of that really bothered you. You had classes and other stuff to worry about. You were in the second half of high school, on the cusp of or just over the line of adulthood when it happened. At the beginning of the year, the very beginning, it was just a little disturbance. In his beginning of the year speech the principal mentioned that the state government had chosen your school as one of the test sites for a &quot;new educational college preparatory standardized educational system&quot; sponsored by Fiber, some &quot;educational technologies&quot; startup you'd never heard of. He tried to make it sound like an honor for the school, but he crammed the announcement in at the end and almost seemed like he was hurrying past it. Also, he was sweating through the whole speech. And there were guys in dark suits and glasses lurking around. But you got used to all of that. Things were maybe a little weirder, a little louder, a little more dangerous, but what were a few more lacerations and broken bones? Only a few kids disappeared, and it wasn't anyone you knew well. <br /> <br /> And then, one night, when you found yourself staying late at the school for whatever reason, it happened. You heard what sounded almost like an explosion from the woods behind the school, you saw a white flash, and you blacked out for a little. When you woke up, you realized that you weren't actually a high school student. You weren't a teenager or a young adult or an adult or however old you thought you were. You weren't human. You were a creature of metal and plastic and living fire and cameras and wires and gun barrels and cement and eyes, you had been placed in that school to do a job- and you had failed. <br /> <br /> Or: <br /> <br /> - The once-prestigious Long Beach Island Oceanographic Institute is desperate for funds and starts using its small fleet of air and watercraft for a smuggling operation. Essentially, Breaking Bad if Walter had a degree in Marine Biology instead of chemistry.<br /> <br /> And, one I've always wanted to try:<br /> <br /> - Evil carnies. They're one of horror'a favorite go-to enemies. But what's it actually like to be an evil carnie? What are their lives like? Basically, all the players are spooky carnies. Funnel cake is required for each session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 03-04-2016, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T12:58:09-08:00","id":842101,"title":"","content":"- Five children, five countries, five pillars, and five souls, five guardians. In the year 2006, an event occurred. One you may not have heard because it was swept under the rug by shady organizations. Five children, seperated by vast distances around the world vanished without a trace. exactly one year later they were all found comatose on an island aranged in a circle. Scientists were baffled. It's been five years since they were found and now they wake to find themselves in a conflict between warring nations, underground conspiracies, a darkness creeping over the globe, and themselves. <br /> <br /> What will they choose? The fate of existence rests on their choice. The problem? The don't remember what the choice is.<br /> <br /> - College is when things change. It's when you get to turn your life around. That's the way it was for 6 high school friends as they all move to a peaceful little college town to finnally be free. But now they find they can't leave, the school isn't what it appears, and there's an evil beneath the town just itching to get free. Will they escape their cage yet again?<br /> <br /> - A highway to hell had never been so litteral. A single greyhound bus full of passengers going one way or the next crashed. Many passengers died. A few survived. The bus driver swears that there was a body in the middle of the road. The passengers would have liked to know more before disappeared before their eyes. So now they wade through the fog as they pass the city sign reading &quot;Silent Hill&quot;. They hope they find help.<br /> <br /> - They say that nothing happens less than twice. Is that true? For those who've been to Faerie and escaped to tell of it, they sure hope not. But in a city of ruthless rules and lax protection, small club of Changelings might just be the tipping balance in a contract that has been woven and re-woven for over a century. Will they use it in their favor or break it.<br /> <br /> - Ghost stories don't often end well. A lot of people die in them. But when their school starts fluctuating between this realm and that of the dead, 6 friends must brave the school at night and find the truth of it all. They are going to wish they HAD died.<br /> <br /> - No one likes an Infestation. Especially not the Local Ring &quot;Ihr&quot; who see the crytids that having been appearing lately as a beacon for the The Machine. A beacon that must be silenced. It was a simple job, until a very old Hunter Angel returns to seek vengeance against one of the Ihr for past transgressions. Can the Ihr survive a simple clean-up job at the same time as defending and evading a violent angel about ready to fall?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T18:55:29-08:00","id":842330,"title":"","content":"[Changeling/Demon]<br /> It all started on a seemingly normal (or at least, normal as such things go) day, one on which a Ring of Saboteurs had planed a strike against a powerful piece of local Infrastructure. Except, when they arrived, they discovered that something else had struck first. The whole Facility was overrun with growth, thorn-covered vines jamming the gears as strange not-Cryptids roamed the halls, the only of the original occupants still alive a utterly deranged Exile and a newly Fallen, near catatonic Demon. A few days later, a small Motley came across a strange circle of standing stones that left them sluggish and drove the local Hobs into a fearful frenzy as they strove to flee from it. This strange back and forth continued for weeks before a Changeling and a Demon who had forged a working relationship found it pertinent to mention this to one another, and in the resultant conversation managed to work out the truth; the Machine and the Hedge (or perhaps Arcadia or the Wyrd?) have gone to war against each other. <br /> <br /> Now the players and their societies have a unique but perilous opportunity. If they choose to take it, they could try to play their foes against each other, try to keep them balanced and weak, too busy sniping at each other to focus on their former servants. If they fail, however, they may empower one of these forces, giving them the strength to launch a powerful offensive. And there's always a few willing to decide that the enemy of their enemy is an ally if it means that enemy's total defeat in the area, no matter if that means sacrificing the other type of escapees...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T19:32:55-08:00","id":842349,"title":"","content":"-The players play important cultists of a Mummy returned to the sleep of ages; you've got your Israeli assassin-for-hire, the deranged archaeologist, the blind high priestess, your charismatic public figurehead, etc, all tasked with pursuing the cryptic orders of your Deathless master. The vibe is distinctly corporate espionage with an occult edge; globe-trotting missions with arcane objectives and powerful foes. These are the folks who know just enough about the secret world to understand just how fucked they are.<br /> <br /> -Anything set in either post-WW1 Istanbul (when the city was occupied and divided among the victors, much like Berlin would be after WW2) or 1920/30s Shanghai (neon-lit &quot;Paris of the East,&quot; with everyone from exiled White Russians to Imperial Japanese causing trouble) write themselves, and that's before we add in the supernatural!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 03-04-2016, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T19:51:28-08:00","id":842363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/841708-pitch-your-campaign?p=842349#post842349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The players play important cultists of a Mummy returned to the sleep of ages; you've got your Israeli assassin-for-hire, the deranged archaeologist, the blind high priestess, your charismatic public figurehead, etc, all tasked with pursuing the cryptic orders of your Deathless master. The vibe is distinctly corporate espionage with an occult edge; globe-trotting missions with arcane objectives and powerful foes. These are the folks who know just enough about the secret world to understand just how fucked they are.<br /> <br /> Anything set in either post-WW1 Istanbul (when the city was occupied and divided among the victors, much like Berlin would be after WW2) or 1920/30s Shanghai (neon-lit &amp;quot;Paris of the East,&amp;quot; with everyone from exiled White Russians to Imperial Japanese causing trouble) write themselves, and that's before we add in the supernatural!</div> </div> </div> </div>...I misread this at first and thought both of those paragraphs referred to same campaign, and briefly wondered what an Israeli would be doing in the 20s before reading it again. Both ideas sound great, though. The second would also be an excellent setting book or Dark Era. What splats do you think would fit them?<br /> <br /> And the first one could be super fun. I love the idea of all these pulp &quot;tomb robber&quot;-story archetypes in the modern business world. Like The Wolf of Wall Street but with less depravity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T20:30:00-08:00","id":842381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/841708-pitch-your-campaign?p=842363#post842363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...I misread this at first and thought both of those paragraphs referred to same campaign, and briefly wondered what an Israeli would be doing in the 20s before reading it again. Both ideas sound great, though. The second would also be an excellent setting book or Dark Era. What splats do you think would fit them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Occupied Istanbul is begging to be made into a Mummy/Demon crossover setting, which needs to happen at some point just to see how it works. You can also throw in some good Vampire and Hunter stuff with ease.<br /> <br /> Shanghai is a 'literally everything goes in the pot' situation. When the mortal situation is eclectic enough to include Nazi spies, Communist dissidents, Japanese marines, Russian gangsters, and Jewish refugees, there's no excuse not to lump the whole damn supernatural world in there; my end goal is any sort of scene with a Changeling speakeasy in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T18:51:35-08:00","id":844264,"title":"","content":"The chronicle I intend to run once Mage 2ED comes out.<br /> \u200bHumboldt county California, home of Redwoods, hidden pot farms and a dark history of Racial tension and violence, first with the native Wiyot people and later the Chinese. The year is 2013 and the reemerging Wiyot people have just announced their intentions to hold a World Renewal Ceremony on Indian Island, the first since the 1860 Massacre.<br /> The characters are all between the ages of 14 and 17, high school students attending the same school in Eureka and until now that was the only thing they had in common. The game will start with them waking up in the early morning hours (think 2a.m.) lying upon the lawn of their high school, with bruises, torn clothes and chaffing around their wrists as if from some form of bondage. All they will have of the last twelve hours are feverish memories of the five of them being chained in a circle between stone pillars (there will be five characters, one for each path and if I don't have five players, most likely, the extras will not wake up at the school and will instead now be missing) with visions of dancing smoke, shadow, and wolves howling just out of sight. They have each undergone an 'Ancient Lands' style awakening, though in this case it will be based on a series of five books that all tell the same story each from the point of view of one of five protagonists (and Paths).<br /> The only Pentacle Mage in the area is a native Wiyot living on the reservation and she is busy preparing for the coming ceremony. Busy enough that she won't discover the heroes until late in the chronicle, leaving only their different books as their guides.<br /> There will be crossover with Changeling, Werewolf and the Circle of the Crone. The story will revolve around the upcoming ceremony, which requires a representative from each path, and the dark and ancient evil that seeks to preempt it.<br /> The chronicle will begin with a focus on the protagonists trying to figure out what happened to them and this magic thing that has entered their lives. Then will move on to trying to find their missing classmates. Then they will actively struggle against that dark power and the role it intends them to play in its plans and the ceremony.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T05:38:00-08:00","id":844459,"title":"","content":"I'll probably never play a Mummy chronicle - it's a lot of work even without the need retrofit to 2E/CofD rules, and my players aren't too interested in the game. But I've always sorta wanted to run a game that, through (incredibly complex) flashbacks and forwards, jumps between five different settings (each thematically linked to a Pillar) at very different points in time/space that all feed into one another. Given that that sounds horrifying complicated, maybe it's for the best I never actually run it.<br /> <br /> Pulp Noir changeling is something I'm also pretty damn tempted to run. Set in London, probably, as I'm UK-based. I think the Noir themes of omnipresent corruption, vice and mistrust work nicely for changeling, and one can see a changeling PI (who probably has a more official role in the freehold, like Bigby from the Wolf Among Us)... I also quite like the image of changeling speakeasies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T10:35:12-08:00","id":844600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/841708-pitch-your-campaign?p=844459#post844459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll probably never play a Mummy chronicle - it's a lot of work even without the need retrofit to 2E/CofD rules, and my players aren't too interested in the game. But I've always sorta wanted to run a game that, through (incredibly complex) flashbacks and forwards, jumps between five different settings (each thematically linked to a Pillar) at very different points in time/space that all feed into one another. Given that that sounds horrifying complicated, maybe it's for the best I never actually run it.<br /> <br /> Pulp Noir changeling is something I'm also pretty damn tempted to run. Set in London, probably, as I'm UK-based. I think the Noir themes of omnipresent corruption, vice and mistrust work nicely for changeling, and one can see a changeling PI (who probably has a more official role in the freehold, like Bigby from the Wolf Among Us)... I also quite like the image of changeling speakeasies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Love all of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T11:27:26-07:00","id":860449,"title":"","content":"I dislike hunter but I some times want to run a campaign.<br /> The prince of Rio has decided to anex Niter\u00f3i to her domain. The local groups of hunters are being exterminated one by one. There is no victory in here that includes the kindred to be beaten, not now. The changelings are also taking this oportunity to take their freehold back, the few prometheans in niter\u00f3i are indulging in revenge as well, to many of their friends taken away, everyone wants a piece of the hunters. The only way to &quot;win&quot; is either by scaping the city and regroup to take the city back one day. Or. Well. To take as many of them as you can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11165-tangledvirus","name":"TangledVirus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T13:42:21-07:00","id":860539,"title":"","content":"With Dark Eras now out, I'm itching to do a Mage chronicle that heavily involves past lives, flashing back from the modern day to the historical settings. My only barriers to that are finding an in-setting excuse to relive those memories and finding a group willing to play it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T13:48:12-07:00","id":860542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/841708-pitch-your-campaign?p=860539#post860539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Dark Eras now out, I'm itching to do a Mage chronicle that heavily involves past lives, flashing back from the modern day to the historical settings. My only barriers to that are finding an in-setting excuse to relive those memories and finding a group willing to play it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The same reason Philodox is looking back into the Sundered World for the Seers. To uncover the location of a powerful, one of a kind artifact like the Omphalos stones. They may not have always been hidden from Mages, and previous Awakened might hold the key to uncovering where they might be<br /> <br /> from a Storyteller perspective, you could change it based upon what happens to characters in each flashback.<br /> <br /> They could also like, time travel, or some weird combination of the two as a result of an artifact, where their minds are literally cast back in time into the bodies of other Awakened to 'take over.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T14:09:38-07:00","id":860549,"title":"","content":"An Arch-Master appears before you. &quot;Yeah, I have a few favors I'd like you to do for me.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T15:22:29-07:00","id":860588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/841708-pitch-your-campaign?p=860539#post860539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Dark Eras now out, I'm itching to do a Mage chronicle that heavily involves past lives, flashing back from the modern day to the historical settings. My only barriers to that are finding an in-setting excuse to relive those memories and finding a group willing to play it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think of this, too, but <b>Werewolf</b> instead. I like that game but the only way I could be convinced to <i>run</i> it rather than play it is if it was this sort of campaign, although I'm waiting for Forsaken by Rome.<br /> <br /> Still, I'd be interested in playing once <b>Mage 2e</b> arrives if you wanted to do it pbp here or even video/chat.<br /> <br /> Actually you know what'd be great? A Mutapa game where the contemporary Mages explore their past lives in Africa but the Mummy players are the same characters, you know? &quot;Oh, hey Steve. Yeah I remember your incarnation from a couple hundred years ago, you're the same guy just reincarnated. Yeah we had a lot of fun together&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T15:32:12-07:00","id":860593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/841708-pitch-your-campaign?p=860588#post860588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think of this, too, but <b>Werewolf</b> instead. I like that game but the only way I could be convinced to <i>run</i> it rather than play it is if it was this sort of campaign, although I'm waiting for Forsaken by Rome.<br /> <br /> Still, I'd be interested in playing once <b>Mage 2e</b> arrives if you wanted to do it pbp here or even video/chat.<br /> <br /> Actually you know what'd be great? A Mutapa game where the contemporary Mages explore their past lives in Africa but the Mummy players are the same characters, you know? &amp;quot;Oh, hey Steve. Yeah I remember your incarnation from a couple hundred years ago, you're the same guy just reincarnated. Yeah we had a lot of fun together&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You can thank Werewolf for the initial idea; even though I'd scarcely call myself a fan of Forsaken, the Hunting Ground: Sumer thing has stuck in my imagination for ages. <br /> <br /> Hunter/Mummy might be fun for past lives as well; it's why I wrote my little Minor Template, actually! The idea of hunting a foe across several lives until you can actually get it right is a blast, to say nothing of cultists who remember cruelties in previous Descents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T18:14:28-07:00","id":860690,"title":"","content":"Building off the previous ideas, a few proto-campaign Mage ideas that are based off what little I as a non-backer know of Sundered World.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">\u2022Modern-To-Vinca: The pcs are in their Hollow-Sanctum, hanging out or doing business or just sleeping, when there's a sudden <i>lurch</i>, and the next thing they know is that the world outside their door is gone. Instead, the place they were in is now in one of the larger Vinca settlements, surrounded by both Sleepers (who are wondering why this structure is now in the middle of their home) and the local Wise (who are wondering why this structure is now in the middle of their home AND are curious as to how it developed a Hallow overnight). Now our heroes have to learn to survive in a world untamed, bargaining with the locals, discussing the hows and shoulds and cans of altering history, and trying to figure out how they got here and if there are any ways to go back.<br /> <br /> \u2022Vinca-To-Modern: The pcs are Wise who, after some scenes in their village to remind them of what the characters are about to lose, end up taking the wrong turn in a Time-Before ruin and end up wandering into a Hallow in a modern Consilium. The beginning of the chronicle would cover the adjustment period, as the pcs figure out the obvious aspects of what happened, make first contact with the locals, and learn the basics of fitting in in this brave new world (including a lingua franca that Sleepers can understand), preferably becoming embroiled in local shadow politics in the process. Then the story would move onto the living. Do the characters wish to rush to return home, or do they feel they and their people might benefit if they take their time? Can they even go home?<br /> <br /> \u2022Vinca-and-Modern: A somewhat complex and convoluted idea on my part, I'll admit. It starts with the dual-chronicle idea, with players having one character in the Dark Era and another in the modern day. The twist being that the two groups are aware of each other somehow. Maybe they have an Artifact that allows them to send written thought-records at each other. Alternatively, maybe pair each character with another from a different era and player. When one set of characters sleep, they do not dream, but instead find themselves a disembodied voice in another Mage's head (still played by the same player). Sort of like what I've heard about how the Shadow is played in Wraith: the Oblivion, but without the mandate to make the other player's life harder. The first option seems like it'd be easier and require less bookkeeping, however.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T18:26:22-07:00","id":860696,"title":"","content":"Viking Era game where an idigam is working on becoming Valhalla, complete with valkyries gathering the souls of dead warriors and bringing powerful spirits to heel. The only force strong and organized enough to deal with it are the Pure tribes, associated and aligned with the primordial giants.<br /> <br /> So, basically, the Ragnarok. And it might just end the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T20:55:59-07:00","id":860759,"title":"","content":"Post-Apocalyptic Faithful of Shulpae. A small group of drifters wandering the wastes hunting for other groups with supernatural patrons to feast upon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T22:36:45-07:00","id":860800,"title":"","content":"I have a rough idea for the forsaken game I will be running. I've never ran werewolf before. <br /> <br /> So. <br /> In western Washington a city cut into the mountains. <br /> The first forsaken pact made a deal with a powerful spirit for protection from some &quot;thing&quot; the spirits refer to as &quot;the storm of ashen leaves&quot; the rite has to be performed on the last day of winter each year ( not the Calendar date but one as dictated by the current highest rank snow spirit) . In 2015 the rite failed, the sacrifice left untouched. <br /> It started when the first ghost entered the Shadow and then existed again with great ease. More dead became restless the number of them who could traverse tge shadow rapidly increased to the dozens. By the end of Spring The name of the protection spirit was then stripped from lore. That's how the wolves remember it. The next great event was the fires that ravaged Washington in the summer. And then a deadly calm through autumn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11570-vasilios","name":"Vasilios","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11570_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T01:16:23-07:00","id":860856,"title":"","content":"A Campaign hack I've been thinking of....<br /> <br /> Everyone wants Heroes. With the rise of global Fear and cries for something to change, the Mayan calendar slowly ticked on, in 2012 something Broke. The Flood of Fear and Hope reached a peak and summoned something, something that unleashed energies into the world that had previously only appeared in legends, Magic. Inspiration. Infernal and Divine. Feral and Industrial. These powers found and bonded to individuals and empowered them in ways that were Miraculous but Dire, with each of them came a Hunger, a Need. Those that used their new powers found themselves becoming something different then human.<br /> <br /> The powers themselves are already in the World of Darkness... It's just a Way of having different Archetypes linked to them.<br /> Divine Fire: Linked to Inventors and Scientists, allows them to make most sciences work even Theoretical ones. The Hunger Linked to them is the need for Knowledge and the Need to use their Science more and More... Consuming their own hopes and dreams.. Burning them out into a Husk of nothing but Madness and Knowledge. The only thing that keeps them Stable is Reason.<br /> Spiritual Communion: Linked to Naturalists and the Deeply Religious. Allows for the calling of Miracles and communion with Nature. The Hunger for them is &quot;Restoring the Natural Order&quot; by placing humans as Prey or forcing them into Worship of the Spirits. The only thing keeping them Stable is Faith.<br /> Deathless Harrowing: Linked with anyone who Works with the Dead or Dying, allows them to Communicate with ghosts and bind flesh. Their Hunger is slow, they feel the need to become closer to the dead and feed upon the living to let them learn what the Dead feel. The only thing keeping them Stable is Hope.<br /> <br /> Their is more... But you get the Idea. Mixing Superheroics with Legends and Ancient myth while dealing with the horror of being something other then Human from now on.. and Not having a Culture to help you adapt to the new needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T00:50:20-07:00","id":862500,"title":"","content":"Boston, present day. The world is mourning Great Britain, having mostly burned in a horrifying anti-establishment revolt years before. The City on the Hill has gotten quieter, more still, more safe. The cost of all that change is fear. There are things going bump in the night, and people are starting to catch on. The lot of you are summoned together by the Handler, an enigmatic man with the ashes of London smoldering in his mournful eyes. He seems to learn new things about you just by looking you over, and knows a lot about you on top of that. For instance, you have no allegiances, hardly any ties to your respective communities, and most importantly none of you seem to care about the disparate supernatural natures each other displays. He needs all that, and he has offers seemingly tailor-made for you, which you take. His eerie assistant <s>who you swear has kuzdu vines laced through her hair when you see her out of the corner of your eye</s> smiles mirthlessly at you as she <s>demands your compliance with a rapier to your back</s> gives you your marching orders, and sends you adventuring <s>to your well-deserved deaths, and you will never deserve to take orders from this glorious man no matter how much he wants to trust you</s> into the night. <s>He will always trust me more than he will trust all of you. Do not forget that.</s><br /> <br /> The changeling freehold in Waltham is scrambling for sanity. In some part, because the Master of the Spring Court has been murdered. Some, like the Master of the Summer Court, just think he was an idiot who is dumb enough to be dead. Others, like the Mistress of the Autumn Court, fear that the Winter King had him assassinated in efforts to delay the end of Winter and bring Boston to a grinding halt under a quilt of snow. All three opposing courts are preparing to engage in full-scale war to prevent the Unrelenting Blizzard that would come with Winter's absolute rule. However, the bigger part is that all of the Fae lords and ladies on the other side of Boston's region of the Hedge are very, messily dead. No one knows who or what did it, but everyone wonders what happens when something that obscenely potent wants to enter Boston from Arcadia....<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the vampire court erupting out of Boston's Financial District is on the look-out for a very specific vampire. He's 5'10&quot;, chalk white skin, wiry build, kind of a douche, smiles all the time, doesn't give a damn about the Masquerade, not in an eating-people-in-front-of-people kind of way but rather a &quot;yo you heard of Mos Def I'm his cousin Mos Feratu haha holla&quot; kind of way. The Prince (Nosferatu, grouchy, loves to read, irritated by anything that gets in the way of her reading, is also a secretly-terrifying power player who is rumored to have disappeared the last Prince and most of her political rivals in the course of a week) is superbly irritated by this. The problem is, whenever this guy's brought in front of the Court for a tribunal, he puts a spring in everyone's step. He's got people chuckling under their breath and whistling showtunes with him. What's more, the more ancient a vampire is, the more they're under his... thrall? It's not like he's actively whammying other Kindred, it's just that they seem to gain the capacity for happiness and joy when he's around. He makes vampire friends, and that is WEIRD. The Danse Macabre ceases to exist in his presence, and no one knows what to make of it. At least, until they're IN his presence, when it actually seems like a great idea all of the sudden! Soon, everyone is falling over themselves to get him for their own reasons. The Carthians want him to break Progeny hardcore and usher in a new vampiric golden age. The Ordo Dracul believe he has achieved Golconda and want to study him. And what's left of the local Invictus just want him stone-dead. Of course, he has other (really misguided) ideas, and he'd like your help.<br /> <br /> Werewolves and sin-eaters have found reasons to work together in the middle of this madness. Packs and krewes get together and have long heartfelt talks about their hopes, dreams, and aspirations. They get some real bonding done! It's pretty great until all the Loci and Avernian Gates start snapping shut. Have the Pure come down from the White Mountains to ruin everyone's day? Are the local mages making some kind a power play? Or does it have something to do with the throng of stiffly-moving empty-eyed little ballet dancers, smelling strangely of crematory ash mixed with porcelain, who don't seem to have homes or souls?<br /> <br /> The mages? Usually the novices all dress up like Gandalf the Gray at least a few times a month, crash at least one vampire club, and ironically dance like morons. The local Prince after all has banned directly interacting with mages down to making smirking eye contact, so it's a fun way for them to piss everyone in attendance off. But now, nothing. They've been keeping to themselves. That is probably bad. Your Handler recommends looking into it.<br /> <br /> Other mysteries abound. What's with the shady pharmaceutical conglomerate buying up <s>cursed</s> condemned buildings, leveling them, and building nothing on top? Have all the mundane human crime organizations banded together to fight back against the things that hide in the shadows and screw with their money (hint: you will probably find out the hard way)? Who is the Gestalt, and why are there so many of him all over the city at once? What is the Screaming Tunnel? Does the terrifying Blood Sister of the Blue Hills Pack really think that macaroni art is the key to overcoming kuruth? Why hasn't the Mayor been seen outside of City Hall for the past two months?<br /> <br /> All this and MORE, when I can finally get a group of four-to-five people I want to play with to sit down in a room at the same time every-other-week. :\\","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5236-lackey-man-ren","user":"Lackey Man Ren","date":". 04-09-2016, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5236-lackey-man-ren","name":"Lackey Man Ren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T16:28:30-07:00","id":889441,"title":"","content":"<b>Brave New World</b><br /> Something's gone terribly wrong. One day, out of the blue, the world shook, a terrible <i>CRACK</i> echoed throughout the city, and the sky shattered, revealing an alien firmament above. Both the mundane and supernatural community panicked, especially when it was discovered the world around the city had become a vast wilderness inhabited by flora and fauna that are very much not native to Earth. The state of the various links to the other worlds would depend on the gamelines be used. But now the city is in chaos, and someone needs to rally the people so they can survive and potentially figure out what's going on. Will you be willing to step up to the plate? Even if it means potentially exposing yourself to the people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T15:50:05-07:00","id":890207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/841708-pitch-your-campaign?p=860539#post860539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Dark Eras now out, I'm itching to do a Mage chronicle that heavily involves past lives, flashing back from the modern day to the historical settings. My only barriers to that are finding an in-setting excuse to relive those memories and finding a group willing to play it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd play that game, but I'd probably play any WoD/CofD game I didn't have to run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T17:17:50-07:00","id":890271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/841708-pitch-your-campaign?p=860539#post860539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Dark Eras now out, I'm itching to do a Mage chronicle that heavily involves past lives, flashing back from the modern day to the historical settings. My only barriers to that are finding an in-setting excuse to relive those memories and finding a group willing to play it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was considering something similar to this for Vampire; a coterie of disenfranchised down-and-out neonate outsiders reluctantly volunteers for an Ordo experiment in gleaning genealogical and personal insights from the characters' bloodlines (not Bloodlines) from close study of blood sympathy.<br /> <br /> It failed wildly at its intended goal. However, it <i>has </i>Butterfly Effect-ed their consciousnesses into their distant proto-sires Torpid bodies. When the characters' blood sympathy leads them back to one another, they pop home. From then on, whenever any one of them goes into Torpor, they all do, and find themselves back in their proto-sires' lives.<br /> <br /> The whole thing would revolutionize kindred culture and occultism if only the damn researcher could be convinced it was more than a shared past-life fantasy communicated to one another by accident.<br /> <br /> Also, the Fog of Ages makes a triumphant return as a literal fog that scents and hunts time travelers a la the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hounds_of_Tindalos\" target=\"_blank\">Hounds of Tindalos</a>. It gets persistently more aggressive if the characters start cross-contaminating timelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T03:19:53-07:00","id":890523,"title":"","content":"Hastur, that's bizarre and I love it. Especially the Fog-as-Hound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T19:11:46-07:00","id":891512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/841708-pitch-your-campaign?p=890523#post890523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hastur, that's bizarre and I love it. Especially the Fog-as-Hound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I like historical-into-modern games, but I don't like trading out and aging NPCs over and over, or keeping track of timeline changes. I figured I could get the best of both via Quantum Leap into a <i>very </i>distant past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T16:54:35-07:00","id":892118,"title":"","content":"I tend to be more of a 20 minutes into the future kind of guy as opposed to historical, but lately, I've got it in my head to try a rather interesting setting...<br /> <br /> <br /> [Any]<br /> Imagine an underwater city, somewhere in the heart of the Atlantic at the bottom of the depths. Founded via a coalition of government and businesses, this city was founded to ensure humanity's future would be a prosperous one. It is self sufficient and derives power from natural sources, growing a promising city-state beneath the waves within a decade.<br /> <br /> In here, people live about these massive spires of arcologies, each practically a city district in both size and function. Yet where there is people, the monsters aren't far behind. People think they're safe, unable to be harmed and seperate from the worries in dangers in top side. This model city of the future features advanced industries suited for underwater work and public transportation services, Artificial intelligence have been developed and are considered &quot;free citizens&quot; within its borders, and it pioneers in advanced robotics for industrial and security use as traditional vehicles were too limited in their use.<br /> Wi-Fi signals are broadcasted everywhere via hotspots, though independant and secure broadcasts, especially from the outside are unheard of. Space is surprisingly roomy in most public areas, but there's enough walls and service shafts to get lost anywhere and into the jaws of some creature.<br /> <br /> It seemed like a veritable city of tommorrow, but the crime rates are still so high and poverty just seems like it is everywhere. People blame smuggling. The truth is, they built a cage... and locked themselves inside. <br /> Vampires still draw blood, Werewolves still claim territory, Mages still seek mysteries, and other stranger things lurk in the walls and ventilation. There might be robotic drones and security cameras keeping watch, but not enough of them everywhere and anyone with the right knowhow can basically remove them from the equation.<br /> Even worse, there's rumors around the city that its inception was not some noble goal but the hinting of something far darker and more sinister....<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 05-16-2016, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T17:08:10-07:00","id":892127,"title":"","content":"@Almarck: Utopia Now done messed up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T17:20:25-07:00","id":892135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/841708-pitch-your-campaign?p=892127#post892127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Almarck: Utopia Now done messed up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Who were they again? <br /> <br /> <br /> I should perhaps mention that there's some serious body modifications available to make a normal man superhuman with enough money paid to the right people, ranging from musclar enhancements, cybernetics, &quot;brain phones&quot;, nanomachine hives, geneware and so on. Available only here and are quite controvertial, especially due to a variety of accusations being flung around by other, less successful surface based competitors.<br /> <br /> ... I really need to assemble a minor template all about that and upgrade my playable AI rules if I ever want to run this. Fortunately, the whole city being a giant computer system built to accomodate AIs, I'm sure that there's a way to put them in &quot;public access&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T17:27:22-07:00","id":892139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/841708-pitch-your-campaign?p=892135#post892135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who were they again? </div> </div> </div> </div>A Hunter Compact introduced in Mortal Remains; they're a start-up with Randian/Objectivist leanings who disassemble Infrastructure and location-based Angels in order to reverse-engineer their processes. One of their goals was to create a self-sufficient little utopia out at sea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T02:29:41-07:00","id":892394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/841708-pitch-your-campaign?p=892118#post892118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to be more of a 20 minutes into the future kind of guy as opposed to historical, but lately, I've got it in my head to try a rather interesting setting...<br /> <br /> <br /> [Any]<br /> Imagine an underwater city, somewhere in the heart of the Atlantic at the bottom of the depths. Founded via a coalition of government and businesses, this city was founded to ensure humanity's future would be a prosperous one. It is self sufficient and derives power from natural sources, growing a promising city-state beneath the waves within a decade.<br /> [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>Smells of both God Machine and Bioshock for miles...<br /> I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T00:23:25-07:00","id":897623,"title":"","content":"Neolithic era mentions a Spirt of War from the future. It occurs to me that it might be interesting to do a Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:54:15-07:00","id":897991,"title":"","content":"[Innocents -&gt; Geist]<br /> In an abandoned theme park, a bunch of kids had to deal with some unsettling, unknowable terror. It marked all of them. 20 years later, those kids are now adults, and all have made the Bargain and come back to their hometown. And the thing in the park was just the beginning.<br /> <br /> [Werewolf]<br /> The pack is totemed with the Great Snake, a spirit embodying Route 66. They are a motorcycle gang, traveling back and forth across the US.<br /> <br /> [Beast]<br /> Think Desperate Housewives meets Buffy meets Orphan Black. A real focus on the real lives of these characters, and letting their hungers guide the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5985-jessel","name":"Jessel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5985_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T13:13:52-07:00","id":898143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jessel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/841708-pitch-your-campaign?p=897991#post897991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Innocents -&gt; Geist]<br /> In an abandoned theme park, a bunch of kids had to deal with some unsettling, unknowable terror. It marked all of them. 20 years later, those kids are now adults, and all have made the Bargain and come back to their hometown. And the thing in the park was just the beginning.<br /> <br /> [Werewolf]<br /> The pack is totemed with the Great Snake, a spirit embodying Route 66. They are a motorcycle gang, traveling back and forth across the US.<br /> <br /> [Beast]<br /> Think Desperate Housewives meets Buffy meets Orphan Black. A real focus on the real lives of these characters, and letting their hungers guide the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm stealing that Werewolf plot if I ever run it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T13:24:44-07:00","id":898149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/841708-pitch-your-campaign?p=898143#post898143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm stealing that Werewolf plot if I ever run it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feel free! With how much I love so many of the other game lines, my Werewolf pitch will probably never end up happening. I'm happy to see it live somewhere else!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5985-jessel","name":"Jessel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5985_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T14:14:56-07:00","id":898204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jessel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/841708-pitch-your-campaign?p=897991#post897991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think Desperate Housewives meets Buffy meets Orphan Black.</div> </div> </div> </div>That post is getting a Like just for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T14:41:35-07:00","id":898236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/841708-pitch-your-campaign?p=898204#post898204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That post is getting a Like just for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha, thanks! I really really really like the idea of watching a Minotaur, a Medusa, and a Dragon all drinking on their patio and angry at each other for having sex with the other one's pool boy or not doing the PTA bake sale like she PROMISED she would last Wednesday ... and also having to go kill the mail man's dog to feed the insatiable hunger inside them.<br /> <br /> And then the pool boy slides a knife into the ribs of the Beast he's having an affair with because he saw her that one time flip over the Prius in the parking lot of the Target late one night and hasn't been able to stop thinking about it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5985-jessel","name":"Jessel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5985_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T15:07:21-07:00","id":898271,"title":"","content":"<b>The A. Nigma Academy for Exceptional Youth</b><br /> <br /> You're honestly not sure how it happened. One day, all across the continent, the world went insane, dissolving into a nightmarish blend of symbols and colors and hallucinations like a very bad drug trip no one over 18 could see. Then it was over, but you were drawn deeper in, dragged or lured on a strange quest where you signed your name and unlocked a strange power. That's when the recruiters came.<br /> <br /> They assured you what happened was, if not normal, then nothing to be alarmed of. They explained what it meant to be Awakened, and how many young people like yourself had journeyed to the Watchtowers, and how more had been uplifted into Proximi. They even gave you a full ride scholarship to a special school for people just like you, so you could learn to use your power for its rightful purpose. It's an offer you <b>can't</b> refuse.<br /> <br /> The Throne doesn't deal well with rejection, you see.<br /> <br /> So now that you've accepted or had &quot;sense&quot; beaten into you, you have been escorted to an isolated and luxurious institution where your Awakening classifies you as the cream of the crop. Organized first into classes and then into junior Pylons, you'll have to not just be clever, cunning and powerful to survive; you'll have to work together to achieve your goals.<br /> <br /> Especially if that goal is escaping and surviving. Or figuring out things, like how these &quot;Pentacle&quot; Mages you've heard rumors about failed to recruit any of the new Awakened, or even what actually happened that day the world went mad...<br /> <br /> <b>TL;DR:</b> Basically, &quot;Wizard School&quot; meets &quot;Academy for Supervillains&quot;, as you play a bunch of newly Awakened 13-18 year olds press-ganged as Seers in the wake of a bizarre mass Awakening.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":". 05-24-2016, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T15:19:15-07:00","id":898285,"title":"","content":"I briefly mentioned this elsewhere, but I'd love to do a Mage game wherein all of the player characters are Seers, just to explore what things are like on the other side of the fence. If it needs a stronger framing dvice than that, then playing through the power struggles between Pantechnion and Mammon for the patronage of the Chancellor, and then whoever wins that trying to oust Hegemony from power in order to secure an Archgenitor seat and the title of Great Ministry.<br /> <br /> I'm also puzzling out the idea of a crossover game set in Hawaii, in order to explore Polynesian mythology and to highlight the fascinating international crime that happens there yet rarely gets mentioned. Is it mostly an excuse to have an Extempore born from a volcanic eruption? Duh, but there's enough meat there for plenty else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T12:02:14-07:00","id":901232,"title":"","content":"Here's the pitch I sent my group for Changeling/Geist set on Mars:<br /> <br /> ____________________<br /> <br /> We got to Mars and it wasn't what we thought.<br /> <br /> The planet was conquered by corporate boots before any countries ever got to it, and they claimed the orbit, the ultimate high ground, and bought prisoners and the poverty-stricken by the boatload, marked them, chipped them, and put them to work digging in the red soil. They they found out there's life out in the rocks. You dig too deep for water or warm up enough of the ground and it stirs. Sticks in the life support. Red weed chokes your water scrubbers. Water seekers breed uncontrollably in anything open. The rust gets into your boots, your eyes, your soul. Crawls into you while you work, makes you something different, not just in your eyes but in the eyes of everyone who's never seen a salmon pink sunrise or had to go into debt just to buy another twenty-four hours of air for your family.<br /> <br /> When the first fighting started, it was put down quickly by the robots the companies sent in. After that, wars were human against machine. You helped tear them apart, learned to live with AI overwatch, or learned to take the fighting outside, into the frosty deserts. The companies pressed their advantages, rained down death in the form of captured meteors onto anyone who let out so much as a pirate radio peep. Maybe you're new here, got shipped in with the last batch to replace dead miners or pacified freedom fighters or whatever else might have cropped up on somebody's daily. You have a caseworker sitting at a desk in high orbit making sure your stay is an unpleasant one. The fighting's never stopped.<br /> <br /> You could stay, pick up a laser drill, go into an elevator and down into the rocks, chipping away at the god of war one little piece of gravel at a time. Get another day of clean air and another gallon of water, minus expenses on behalf of the company for letting you live. Live in a dirty hab with wall shine to make you forget how long and hard the day really was. Take the elevator again. Dig until the debt chips away at your body, your mind, your soul.<br /> <br /> You could try leaving, taking a suit and chasing down some abandoned hab you could fix up, but the rocks, they say, lead you the wrong way. Every scattered field of rubble looks like every other field. The same butterscotch sky in every direction. Before you know it you're lost in canyons or old river beds or volcanic crevasses while the rocks honed to a razor's edge by the wind tear into your suit, your skin, your soul.<br /> <br /> It'll make you a whole new person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","user":"raygungoth","date":". 05-27-2016, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T10:28:21-07:00","id":908420,"title":"","content":"I came up with the idea of a whole fictional island nation as a ChroD crossover setting- a country that's only been recently established, a lot of political turmoil, incredible diverse of nationalities and cultures, a U.S. naval base so there's an excuse for TFV to be around, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T23:01:52-07:00","id":908913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/841708-pitch-your-campaign?p=908420#post908420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I came up with the idea of a whole fictional island nation as a ChroD crossover setting- a country that's only been recently established, a lot of political turmoil, incredible diverse of nationalities and cultures, a U.S. naval base so there's an excuse for TFV to be around, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Over_the_Edge_%28game%29#Setting\" target=\"_blank\">Al Amarja</a> welcomes you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3771-damoqles","name":"damoqles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T13:31:02-07:00","id":909425,"title":"","content":"<b>Long May You Reign</b><br /> The first thing you notice when you wake up in the morning is the servant. The funny thing is, you don't <i>have</i> a servant, and if you do, it isn't them. Yet they seem to think they've served you for years, and that there's nothing abnormal about the wealth and opulence surrounding you.<br /> <br /> Investigation reveals the the world is just a <i>tiny bit</i> different than it was when you last went to sleep. More specifically, your kind (or kinds, if running a multi-splat game) rules the nations of the world and always has. You stand among the masters of the strongest of this warped world's nations, whether it be the United Hells of America or the Kingdom of*Cauchemar or even the mighty Threefold Nile Necrocracy. The relevant antagonist groups (The Seers, The G-M, or the Pure, for example) are not so much gone as in hiding, though that does not mean they're not dangerous.<br /> <br /> You're not alone, of course; a few others remember the world the way you do, and fate has placed you all in close proximity. You'll have to work together to figure out what's going on. It's not all bad, when you think about it; most of the populace either reveres or fears you, and you have a vast amount of wealth and power. Of course, it's not all good; in the end you're expected to <b>rule</b>, and your enemies still lurk in the shadows waiting to strike. You'll have to immerse yourself in this world and its politics if you want to get to the bottom of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T19:18:10-07:00","id":925633,"title":"","content":"Here's my next one:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://scontent-ord1-1.xx.fbcdn.net/t31.0-8/q85/s960x960/10495028_723412717770741_9128851407596043377_o.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T06:16:30-07:00","id":925852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/841708-pitch-your-campaign?p=925633#post925633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's my next one:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://scontent-ord1-1.xx.fbcdn.net/t31.0-8/q85/s960x960/10495028_723412717770741_9128851407596043377_o.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Beast? Leviathans?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T11:25:25-07:00","id":925991,"title":"","content":"Nah, just some jiggering with the base rules. The way I'm going to work it is that players will have two characters. One is &quot;human scale&quot; and the other is &quot;kaiju scale.&quot; They'll play their human most of the time, but when the climax rolls around or a big battle is going to break loose, they'll either strap themselves into their robot, undergo trasnformation, or just point out at the ocean and go &quot;look, it's Magmasaur!&quot; and then they'll swap character sheets. If you're a kaiju and something is &quot;human scale,&quot; you break it.<br /> <br /> Masers are human scale weapons that do kaiju damage. That way they can ping you for one or two health at a time, but you can just smash them if you step on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T14:38:13-07:00","id":926091,"title":"","content":"If you don't include merits enforcing the Friend To Children trope I will personally throw <i>such a fit</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T23:51:39-07:00","id":926296,"title":"","content":"Ooh, that's a good idea. How about a merit literally called &quot;Friend to Children&quot; that lets you detect children in peril within some miles based on your Willpower and whenever you use a k-scale attack on or near a building it can't hurt any kids?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}